      "citation_text": "Mont. Code Ann. § 41-3-427(1)(d), (2) — the court grants an order for immediate protection and emergency protective services, including temporary medical or out-of-home care, on probable cause, or on clear and convincing evidence if the case is subject to the federal Indian Child Welfare Act or the Montana Indian Child Welfare Act; same standard as § 41-3-422(5)(a)(i)",
      "source_url": "https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/mca/title_0410/chapter_0030/part_0040/section_0270/0410-0030-0040-0270.html",
